  "id": "Compound::DB00975 - Gene::5137",
  "verbalization": "Dipyridamole is implicated in the regulation of Pde1c through a series of interconnected molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Dipyridamole binds to Pde1a and Pde1b, which are both involved in calmodulin-dependent cyclic-nucleotide phosphodiesterase activity. This activity is ultimately participated by Pde1c, indicating a potential functional relationship between Dipyridamole and Pde1c. The binding of Dipyridamole to Pde1a and Pde1b may modulate the activity of Pde1c, suggesting a role in the regulation of cyclic nucleotide metabolism. The consistent involvement of Pde1c in these pathways, despite the different target proteins, highlights a broader mechanism by which Dipyridamole could influence Pde1c activity. The evidence supports a plausible link between Dipyridamole and Pde1c, mediated through the regulation of calmodulin-dependent phosphodiesterases.",
